.env*
*.db
__pycache__/
tests/
docs/

# vercel.json sets includeFiles "**" for the Python function, so anything sitting at the repo
# root is uploaded into the bundle. These hold plaintext redeemable share tokens. They are
# already gitignored, which is exactly why they were easy to miss here — .gitignore keeps them
# out of the repository, and this file is what keeps them out of the deployment.
#
# Measured 2026-09-17: the API project serves no static files — every repo-root path returns
# 404 and only /api/* exists — so nothing was ever reachable over HTTP. This is about what
# travels in the bundle, not about a leak that happened.
joincode*.txt
demo-secrets.txt

# The front end is its own Vercel project, deployed from git. The Python function has never
# needed a byte of it.
web/
